  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adaptation and mitigation of climate effects for agriculture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adopting sustainable forest resource management strategies aligned along three axes: i) Environmental education actions promoted for the preservation of forest resources and others associated with them; ii) Promoted sustainable agricultural practices in family production units and; iii) Forest recovery and conservation actions promoted. This holistic approach to adaptation (education) and mitigation of the effects of climate change aims to increase the resilience of the poorest and most vulnerable rural communities in the current climate context of Huambo. Therefore, environmental education will be carried out through lectures, debates, awareness campaigns, exchanges, and technical assistance to families. Also to strengthen the agrarian systems of the communities with the introduction of sustainable agricultural practices, forest polygons, and the use of community knowledge and experiences.</narrative>
  </description>
